{"title":"Neuro-Rehab Therapist Roadmap","role":"Neuro-Rehab Therapist","summary":"A Neuro-Rehab Therapist supports the rehabilitation of individuals with neurological conditions that affect movement, balance, coordination, strength, mobility, and functional independence.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Physiotherapy – Sports / Neuro / Paediatric Rehabilitation"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Neuro-Rehab Therapist supports the rehabilitation of individuals with neurological conditions that affect movement, balance, coordination, strength, mobility, and functional independence."},{"type":"p","text":"The professional works as part of a multidisciplinary rehabilitation team that may include physiotherapists, occupational therapists, speech and language professionals, neurologists, rehabilitation physicians, psychologists, and nurses."},{"type":"p","text":"Typical responsibilities include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Neurological movement and functional assessment"},{"text":"Mobility and balance assessment"},{"text":"Strength and range-of-motion assessment"},{"text":"Gait assessment"},{"text":"Therapeutic exercise"},{"text":"Functional mobility training"},{"text":"Balance and coordination training"},{"text":"Post-stroke rehabilitation"},{"text":"Neurodevelopmental rehabilitation"},{"text":"Patient and caregiver education"},{"text":"Progress documentation"},{"text":"Supporting multidisciplinary rehabilitation plans"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Scope note","text":"“Neuro-Rehab Therapist” is often a specialization or job title rather than a universally standardized standalone profession. Clinical practice should be based on the underlying recognized qualification, applicable professional registration, institutional scope, and supervision requirements."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"t